{"qas": [
  {"question": "According to arXiv 2503.05787, how does the EU AI Act propose to address information sharing challenges and what standards are recommended for interoperability?", "answer": "The EU AI Act proposes a foundational ontology for information sharing and recommends semantic web standards for interoperability.", "evidence": [{"page": 9, "quote": "we require a common foundational ontology aligned with the AI Act itself that provides common terminology and basis for developing further approaches"}, {"page": 9, "quote": "the best solution is the use of standards-based information models and processes developed to share them - specifically semantic web standards (World Wide Web Consortium 2024) and their use in data portals"}]},
  {"question": "In arXiv 2503.05787, what is the relationship between regulatory learning and the reduction of reporting obligations in the EU?", "answer": "Regulatory learning is argued to harmonise compliance, supporting the EU's aim to reduce reporting obligations by 25% without weakening protections.", "evidence": [{"page": 9, "quote": "the recent Draghi report outlined reduction in regulatory reporting as one of the key factors essential to ensuring EU competitiveness, and where the Commission's response agrees with this view as it has tabled an 'omnibus regulation' in its agenda for the 2025 work program that reduces reporting and red-tape by 25%."}, {"page": 9, "quote": "our argument for using regulatory learning as a tool to systematise compliance processes across the ecosystem and across regulations should be considered an important factor for such future policy-making decisions."}]},
  {"question": "According to arXiv 2503.05787, what does the abbreviation 'GPAI' refer to in the context of the AI Act's organisational learning activities table?", "answer": "In the table, 'GPAI' refers to General Purpose AI.", "evidence": [{"page": 8, "quote": "g: Revise GPAI threshold and criteria in Anx XIII [52,97] DA"}]},
  {"question": "In arXiv 2503.05787, what is the purpose of the '↔' symbol in the meta-learning activities table?", "answer": "The '↔' symbol indicates bidirectional or mutual relationships between activities in the table.", "evidence": [{"page": 8, "quote": "| a: Develop harmonised standards [40]                                                             | ↔                                          | ↔                                          | ↔                                          | ↔                                          | ↔                                          | ↔                                          | ↔                                          | ↔                                        | ↔                                        | ↔                                        | ↔                                        | ↔                                        | ←                                        | ←                                        |"}]},
  {"question": "Which international bodies are suggested in arXiv 2503.05787 for developing agreements on information exchange for the AI Act, without using the document's exact phrasing?", "answer": "ISO/IEC, CEN/CENELEC, and W3C are recommended for creating information exchange agreements.", "evidence": [{"page": 9, "quote": "we envision the reuse of existing standardisation processes, such as in ISO/IEC, CEN/CENELEC, and W3C to develop appropriate agreements on information exchange formats and processes based on using them."}]},
  {"question": "What is one example given in arXiv 2503.05787 of a standardised ontology used for interoperable data modelling in the EU, described without repeating the document's distinctive wording?", "answer": "The EU's eProcurement Ontology is cited as a standard for modelling procurement data and processes.", "evidence": [{"page": 9, "quote": "Another example is the EU's eProcurement Ontology (Publications Office 2024) which provides a standardised ontology of concepts for interoperable modelling of procurement data and processes based on EU regulations and directives."}]}
]}
